3. What the catalog redistributes
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

All of the mathematical content in the catalog and its dataset is the work of
QuAIR and the Lean-QIT authors:

  * 9,696 declaration names
  * 9,696 type signatures and their binder structure
  * 6,946 documentation strings, reproduced verbatim
  * the module and namespace organisation of the library
  * every theorem, definition, structure, instance and constructor described

The contribution of this project is the extraction and the interface: a
pipeline that reads the library and produces a structured dataset, a reference
index, a search index, and a website for browsing them.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Statement of changes (Apache-2.0 section 4(b))
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No Lean source file was modified. The library was extracted and reformatted:

  * Extracted with doc-gen4, the Lean documentation generator, from Lean-QIT at
    commit da54e3070298468dc884877726bc45a92c57e4b3, built against Lean
    toolchain v4.30.0 and the matching Mathlib revision.

  * doc-gen4 produced a SQLite database whose rendered-type column is a
    length-prefixed binary format. That column was decoded and serialised to
    JSON Lines, downloadable from the catalog website.

  * Docstrings are reproduced verbatim. Signatures are the type as doc-gen4
    rendered it. Neither is altered.

  * Added by this project: the extraction itself, the decoder, the structured
    binder and type-reference fields, and the catalog interface at
    https://leanqit-catalog.pages.dev

  * No mathematical content was altered, corrected, abridged or reinterpreted.

